    rdf:value """[ Monte Senario]
x Monday, Nov. 18, 1895, Fiesole 
Still this marvellous weather, with the best elements of Spring, Summer and Autumn combined.
Miss Paget came to call, and was  especially  nice, talking about music, and how it was all movement, and should stimulate rhythms in the physiological system. 
* Tuesday, Nov. 19, 1895 
We started out at 930 and walked for three hours, almost reaching Monte Senario, a glorious walk. Then we ate our lunch on the hillside and lay down in the grass and smoked, “overlooking the valley.” It was a landscape painted on a huge Chinese screen, the valleys all in pale mist, with only the hill tops emerging, simple and monochrome, a simplicity and beauty European artists """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 27 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1895-96> .

